  "name": "ring",
  "description": "*ring* is a high-performance, general-purpose cryptographic library for Rust that prioritizes safety, speed, and suitability for constrained environments. It exposes a focused set of primitives—including AEAD, RSA, and Elliptic Curve operations—using a hybrid architecture of safe Rust wrappers, optimized C code, and hand-tuned assembly derived from BoringSSL. The implementation emphasizes constant-time execution and a robust API design to prevent common cryptographic pitfalls in systems-level applications.",
